From d8496ddebfc97626e61275dcf0f9b57017434747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 05:34:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Index: Profit stands out, the drawdown/CTA lines, MNQ/NQ ->
 MNQ

Ported onto origin/main's c2b5e50 (RoDD's size bump dropped, faint column
separators added -- pure CSS, replicated manually), carrying everything
from aft-mnq-lineup-v4 (647d218). All four changes are scoped to the index
page per the owner's ask (rebuild_index.py + main.css):

1. "Net" -> "Profit" on the index table's column header and its <td>s (new
   .sx-net class: bold, accent green, a size step above its neighbours --
   the same shape RoDD used to carry before c2b5e50 normalized it back
   down). It's now the first figure the eye lands on in each row after the
   name. The cover-flow's .cf-gain figure already carried this exact
   treatment (bold/accent/2xl) so nothing changed there. Product pages say
   "Net profit", not bare "Net" -- nothing to rename there for consistency.
2. One generated line directly above the index table, verbatim: "All
   strategies simulated based on a $10,000 or less drawdown."
3. "MNQ/NQ" -> "MNQ" in every generator string that rendered it (docstring,
   meta description, lede, MNQ table title). catalog2.json's one remaining
   hit is `_template_strategy`'s field-doc enumerating valid market CODES
   (MNQ/NQ/MGC/SI/ES as alternatives, not a combined label) -- left as is,
   it isn't the same kind of string.
4. A new visible (not grey-caption) CTA line above the hero's lede: "Select
   any of the profitable strategies below to see the trade details and
   results." Every index row's name already linked to its product page
   (unchanged from the cover-flow-return commit) -- verified, not re-added.

Regenerated in order (gen_pages -> rebuild_index -> gen_plan), css hash
recomputed and restamped on all 18 pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
