-        <div class="pdp-main">
-        <div class="rodd" aria-label="Return-on-drawdown sizing menu">
-  <div class="rodd-head">
-    <span class="rodd-title">Sizing</span>
-    <span class="rodd-fig">750%</span>
-  </div>
-  <p class="rodd-why"><b>RoDD is the metric this catalog is priced on.</b> Profit factor says the engine works;
-  RoDD says what it costs to hold: net profit divided by the worst peak-to-valley drawdown.
-  This system&rsquo;s window: $5.5k net &divide; $700 max drawdown = <b>750%</b>.
-  Slide your drawdown budget &mdash; the projection scales with it, and so does the pain.</p>
-  <input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-1" class="ro-r ro-red"><input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-2" class="ro-r ro-red"><input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-3" class="ro-r ro-amb"><input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-4" class="ro-r ro-ok" checked><input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-5" class="ro-r ro-ok"><input type="radio" name="ro-print" id="ro-print-6" class="ro-r ro-ok">
-  <div class="ro-track" aria-hidden="false"><label for="ro-print-1" class="ro-notch"><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$1k</span></label><label for="ro-print-2" class="ro-notch"><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$2.5k</span></label><label for="ro-print-3" class="ro-notch"><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$5k</span></label><label for="ro-print-4" class="ro-notch ro-notch-rec"><span class="ro-rec">our pick</span><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$10k</span></label><label for="ro-print-5" class="ro-notch"><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$25k</span></label><label for="ro-print-6" class="ro-notch"><span class="ro-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ro-amt">$50k</span></label></div>
-  <div class="ro-outs"><div class="ro-out ro-out-1"><span class="ro-flag">Not built for this size</span> The deepest published max drawdown ($3,600, full record) exceeds a $1k budget &mdash; this sizing would not have survived the sample. Some systems are not meant to run this small.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-2"><span class="ro-flag">Not built for this size</span> The deepest published max drawdown ($3,600, full record) exceeds a $2.5k budget &mdash; this sizing would not have survived the sample. Some systems are not meant to run this small.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-3"><span class="ro-flag">Thin cushion</span> The deepest published drawdown ($3,600, full record) is more than half this budget &mdash; one bad stretch uses most of your room. A drawdown budget of <b>$5k</b> historically returned <b class="ro-ret">~$37,500</b> over the best window. Over the full record, <b>$13,550</b>. Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-4"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Recommended</span> The smallest budget that clears the deepest published drawdown ($3,600, full record). A drawdown budget of <b>$10k</b> historically returned <b class="ro-ret">~$75,000</b> over the best window. Over the full record, <b>$27,100</b>. Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-5">A drawdown budget of <b>$25k</b> historically returned <b class="ro-ret">~$187,500</b> over the best window. Over the full record, <b>$67,750</b>. Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-6">A drawdown budget of <b>$50k</b> historically returned <b class="ro-ret">~$375,000</b> over the best window. Over the full record, <b>$135,500</b>. Past results, not a forecast.</div></div>
-  <p class="ro-note">Linear scaling of the published window; not a projection of future results. See the disclaimer below.</p>
